Privacy Policy for NSWDG Blue Squadron

Last updated: 11/5/2025

1. Introduction

Welcome to NSWDG Blue Squadron (“the Bot”).
This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect information when users interact with the Bot on Discord. By using the Bot, you agree to the terms outlined here. If you do not agree, please stop using the Bot.

2. Information We Collect

The Bot may collect and process the following types of data:

User Data: Usernames, user IDs, and server IDs (for command execution and moderation purposes).

Server Data: Configuration settings, permissions, and command usage history.

Message Content: Only when necessary for executing commands (e.g., moderation logs, command triggers).

The Bot does not log or store private messages (DMs) unless explicitly stated for specific features.

Technical Data: Logs related to uptime, errors, and command performance for debugging and improvement.

3. How We Use Your Data

We use collected data for the following purposes:

To execute and improve Bot functionality.

To save server configurations and preferences.

To ensure moderation, anti-abuse, or logging systems work as intended.

To identify and fix bugs or service issues.

To comply with Discord’s Terms of Service and Developer Policy.

4. Data Storage and Retention

Stored data (such as configurations or logs) is kept only as long as necessary for the Bot’s functionality.

Temporary data (like command triggers or short-term logs) is automatically deleted after 365 days.

You may request data deletion at any time (see Section 7).

5. Data Sharing

We do not sell, trade, or share any user or server data with third parties.
Data may be shared only in these limited cases:

To comply with legal requests or Discord’s policies.

To maintain the Bot’s hosting and performance (e.g., error logging via third-party tools).

6. Security

We use industry-standard methods to protect stored data from unauthorized access, alteration, or disclosure.
However, no online service is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute data security.

7. Your Rights

You may:

Request to view or delete any data related to your account or server.

Request that the Bot forgets your server’s configuration or stored information.

Contact us through Discord support server or email: Mrlion_23@outlook.com to make such requests.

8. Children’s Privacy

The Bot does not knowingly collect data from users under 13 years of age.
If you believe data was collected from a minor, contact us immediately to remove it.

9. Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy at any time.
Changes will be announced via our official support server or bot description page. Continued use of the Bot after changes means you accept the updated terms.

